 ## Background
-Alpha blending in volume rendering was developed by Marc Levoy in 1988, building on the Porter-Duff compositing operators introduced in 1984 [S4, unofficial][S5]. Levoy's work adapted the "over" operator from 2D image compositing to 3D volume rendering, providing a physically based method for accumulating light along rays [S4, unofficial]. It has become the standard compositing technique in direct volume ray casting due to its simplicity and associativity [S5].
+Alpha blending in volume rendering was developed by Levoy in 1988, building on the Porter-Duff compositing operators introduced in 1984 [S4][S1, unofficial]. Levoy's work adapted the "over" operator from 2D image compositing to 3D volume rendering, providing a physically based method for accumulating light along rays [S4]. It has become the standard compositing technique in direct volume ray casting due to its simplicity and associativity [S5, unofficial].
 
